
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I still use <a href="https://textexpander.com/">TextExpander every day</a>. In addition to all the other jobs I&#8217;ve given it over the years, it&#8217;s also become an excellent tool for managing and slinging AI prompts at my various robots. It seems the TextExpander team hasn&#8217;t been sleeping. There are a few notable recent updates.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For years, I&#8217;ve kept a series of snippets that are almost identical, with small differences depending on the circumstances. Now TextExpander has <a href="https://textexpander.com/learn/using/snippets/snippet-fill-ins/conditional-sections">Conditional Sections</a>, so I can put those variations into a single snippet and choose the one I need from a dropdown when it expands. That should let me simplify things a bit.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">They&#8217;ve also added spelling and grammar checking right in the snippet editor. Currently, it&#8217;s just English, but more languages are promised.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It&#8217;s nice to see the gang at TextExpander continuing to improve this great little utility.</p>
